 # Quests, tunnel services and travel
+
+## Aggro departure and stationary homes — October24 candidate
+
+Source5116f9b in E:/EQ_Local_Dev/_worktrees/aggro-zone-cleanup corrects two
+reproduced defects; it is not installed or owner-accepted. Palwar's Lower Guk
+Raid bedroom report used no Feign Death and matches the Thursday run whose
+checkpoint retained clustered knights. The owner returned over an hour later,
+consistent with the logged natural unload; in-game resolution remains unproved.
+Ordinary hate removal does not erase feign memory's recyclable entity IDs.
+Client::ClearFeignMemoryOnDeparture removes only matching NPC memory after
+accepted death and at the end of client destruction. Do not substitute broad
+ClearZoneFeignAggro: shared XTarget counters and unrelated return delays change.
+
+Saved stationary positions formerly became guard homes during NPC::AI_Start.
+Spawn2::Process now normalizes the canonical guard using native SendTo rules,
+then restores the pre-publication pose. It preserves heading, construction spawn
+point, loot/resources, grid/roambox roaming and quest movement; the canonical-row
+lookup is value-initialized for missing-row fallback. Raw canonical Z is unsafe:
+fresh AI_Start corrects ground/water Z before saving its guard.
+
+Managed Raid/Grind checkpoints DO use this loader: LoadZoneState consumes
+NightcapDungeon::LoadCheckpoint, keyed by run UUID. The managed bypass in
+LoadZoneVariablesState is only for zone variables. Query dungeon checkpoints,
+not just zone_state_spawns. An older Raid checkpoint contained two stationary
+knights at one point over200units from home in the owner-confirmed incident run;
+re-entry causality is still unconfirmed.
+Empty zones pause normal NPC processing after their settle window (Lower Guk60s);
+long logout alone does not guarantee all displaced NPCs have walked home.
+
+Tests: test_aggro_departure_native.py and test_zone_state_home_native.py execute
+extracted native paths with pinned entity/mob_ai/xtarget/waypoints helpers.
+Nine Windows and three Linux checks pass; independent review resolved shared
+counters, unrelated delays and ground normalization. Fixtures are not nav-mesh,
+checkpoint-SQL or owner gameplay proof. Build status and exact QA are recorded
+in docs/releases/aggro-zone-cleanup-20261024/{README.md,verification.json,QA.md}.
+Zone rebuild required; no SQL, world-rule, cache or client change. Whole-runtime
+production restart needs current owner authorization; never kill a zone child,
+repop a live dungeon or erase checkpoints/player progress to demonstrate the fix.
+Whole current wiki reviewed; no publication/current-player mechanics change from
+this uninstalled candidate. Preserve the concurrent deployed Hole release.
 
